#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:11
msgid "Residuals Generation and Management"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:13
msgid "Drinking water treatment concentrates solids from the raw water into residual streams. Coagulant precipitation contributes additional solids. The solids contain particles including pathogens present in the raw water as well as dissolved organic matter that is adsorbed to the solids. The solids are removed from the treated water and discharged in residual streams. The two principal residual streams from an AguaClara plant are clarifier sludge purges and filter backwash. This chapter provides methods for estimating their solids loads, water volumes, and discharge characteristics for any plant capacity."
msgstr ""

