#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:91
msgid "If daily turbidity data are available, use Equation :eq:`residuals_total_solids_turbidity` for every turbidity value to estimate the daily solids production. If only a single average estimated turbidity is available, use it to estimate the solids production for a typical day. When averaging the turbidity the resulting coagulant dose is not the same as the dose calculated from the average turbidity because of the cube-root relationship. Because coagulant dose increases with the cube root of turbidity, calculating the dose from average turbidity slightly overestimates average coagulant consumption. This overestimation has a negligible effect on the solids production estimate because the coagulant contribution is small compared to the solids from raw water. :numref:`figure_residuals_solids_production` illustrates the component and total solids-production estimates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:100
msgid "Suspended-solids, coagulant, and total solids production as functions of average raw-water turbidity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:100
msgid "Estimated solids production as a function of average raw-water turbidity. The suspended-solids and coagulant-precipitate contributions use the preliminary coefficients listed above; total solids production is the sum of the two contributions. The dotted construction lines show that an average turbidity of 50 NTU produces approximately 0.0635 kg/m³ of total solids."
msgstr ""

