msgid ":math:`C_s` is estimated solids production per volume of raw water treated, in kg/m³."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:117
msgid "For example, a 70 m³/day plant treating raw water with an average turbidity of 50 NTU generates approximately 4.4 kg of solids per day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:123
msgid "Clarifier Sludge Purges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:125
msgid "AguaClara clarifiers produce water with an average turbidity :math:`T_{\\mathrm{clar}}` of approximately 0.5 NTU. The fraction of the solids production removed by the clarifier is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:127
msgid "f_{\\mathrm{clar}} = \\frac{T_{\\mathrm{in}} - T_{\\mathrm{clar}}}{T_{\\mathrm{in}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:134
#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:152
#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:171
msgid ":math:`f_{\\mathrm{clar}}` is the fraction of generated solids removed in the clarifier, dimensionless;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:135
msgid ":math:`T_{\\mathrm{in}}` is the influent or raw-water turbidity, in NTU; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:136
msgid ":math:`T_{\\mathrm{clar}}` is the clarifier effluent turbidity, in NTU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:138
msgid "For the example above, raw water with a turbidity of 50 NTU produces a clarifier effluent of approximately 0.5 NTU, which corresponds to a clarifier capture fraction of 0.99."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:140
msgid "The clarifier purges remove most of the captured solids except for the case of pristine rivers with very low turbidity. The clarifier purge concentration has not been systematically measured across AguaClara plants. A provisional range of **0.5–10 g/L TSS** may be used for preliminary estimates, **not** as a guaranteed operating range. Purge concentration is highly dependent on the raw water turbidity and dissolved organic matter concentrations. The clarifier purge concentration is expected to be significantly higher than the filter backwash concentration because the clarifier provides an opportunity for consolidation of the captured solids."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:142
msgid "If a fraction :math:`f_{\\mathrm{clar}}` of the total generated solids is removed in the clarifier, the daily purge volume is approximately"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:144
msgid "\\forall_{\\mathrm{clar}} = \\frac{f_{\\mathrm{clar}} M_s}{C_{\\mathrm{clar}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:151
#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:170
msgid ":math:`\\forall_{\\mathrm{clar}}` is the daily clarifier-purge volume, in m³/day;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:153
msgid ":math:`M_s` is the dry-solids mass generated per day, in kg/day; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:154
#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:174
msgid ":math:`C_{\\mathrm{clar}}` is the purge total suspended solids concentration, in kg/m³."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:156
msgid "For example, if :math:`M_s=4.4` kg/day, :math:`f_{\\mathrm{clar}}=0.99`, and :math:`C_{\\mathrm{clar}}=5` kg/m³, the estimated purge volume is :math:`\\forall_{\\mathrm{clar}}=0.87\\ \\mathrm{m^3/day}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:158
msgid "Purge scheduling is being refined. Possible operating strategies include intermittent purges (for example, every 12 hours) for low raw water turbidities and a slow continuous purge. Sludge production and purge volume requirements increase with raw-water turbidity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:160
msgid "Combining Equations :eq:`residuals_daily_clarifier_purge_volume` and :eq:`residuals_daily_solids_mass` gives the daily clarifier purge volume as a function of solids concentration as given in :numref:`figure_residuals_solids_production`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:163
msgid "\\forall_{\\mathrm{clar}} = \\frac{f_{\\mathrm{clar}} V_d C_s}{C_{\\mathrm{clar}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:172
msgid ":math:`V_d` is the raw-water volume treated per day, in m³/day;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:173
msgid ":math:`C_s` is the solids production per volume of raw water treated, in kg/m³; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:176
msgid "Equation :eq:`residuals_daily_clarifier_purge_volume_of_solids_concentration` can be used to estimate the clarifier purge volume for any plant capacity and raw-water turbidity. The purge volume is inversely proportional to the purge concentration, which is expected to vary with raw-water turbidity and dissolved organic matter concentration. The purge volume is directly proportional to the plant capacity and the solids production per unit volume of raw water treated. From :numref:`figure_residuals_solids_production`, the solids production per unit volume of raw water treated increases with raw-water turbidity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:182
msgid "Filter Backwash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:184
msgid "Filter backwash removes solids that pass through clarification and accumulate in the filter. Filtered-water turbidity, :math:`T_{\\mathrm{fi}}`, is expected to be less than 0.1 NTU. For a clarifier effluent turbidity of 0.5 NTU, the filter therefore removes approximately 0.4 NTU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:186
msgid "For a filter whose backwash includes an initial discharge volume followed by discharge at approximately plant flow,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:188
msgid "\\forall_b = \\forall_0 + Q_p t_b"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:195
#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:210
msgid ":math:`\\forall_b` is the backwash volume per event, in m³;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:196
msgid ":math:`\\forall_0` is the initial discharge volume, in m³;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:197
msgid ":math:`Q_p` is the plant flow rate during the subsequent discharge, in m³/s; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:198
msgid ":math:`t_b` is the total backwash duration starting from the initial discharge, in s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:200
msgid "If backwashing occurs every :math:`t_i` seconds of operation, the backwash water fraction is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:202
msgid "F_b = \\frac{\\forall_b}{Q_p t_i}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:209
#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:224
msgid ":math:`F_b` is the fraction of treated water used for backwashing, dimensionless;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:211
#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:225
msgid ":math:`Q_p` is the plant flow rate, in m³/s; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:212
msgid ":math:`t_i` is the time between the start of backwash events, in s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:214
msgid "The average daily backwash volume is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:216
msgid "\\forall_{b,d} = F_b Q_p t_d"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:223
msgid ":math:`\\forall_{b,d}` is the average daily backwash volume, in m³/day;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:226
msgid ":math:`t_d` is the number of operating seconds per day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:228
msgid "**PF70 example.** The ShOStaRS filter is expected to require a backwash every 12–30 hours of operation, depending on raw-water turbidity, coagulant dose, and clarifier performance. The backwash duration is expected to be approximately 15–20 minutes. For this example, use a plant flow of :math:`Q_p=70\\ \\mathrm{m^3/day}`, an initial discharge volume of :math:`\\forall_0=0.200\\ \\mathrm{m^3}`, a backwash duration of :math:`t_b=15\\ \\mathrm{min}`, and an interval of :math:`t_i=18\\ \\mathrm{h}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:230
msgid "Substitution into Equation :eq:`residuals_backwash_event_volume` gives the backwash volume per event:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:232
msgid "\\forall_b\n"
"= 0.200\\ \\mathrm{m^3}\n"
"+ \\left(70\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{m^3}}{\\mathrm{day}}\\right)\n"
"  \\left(15\\ \\mathrm{min}\\right)\n"
"  \\left(\\frac{1\\ \\mathrm{day}}{1440\\ \\mathrm{min}}\\right)\n"
"= 0.929\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{m^3}}{\\mathrm{event}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:242
msgid "Using Equation :eq:`residuals_backwash_water_fraction`, the fraction of treated water used for backwashing is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:244
msgid "F_b\n"
"= \\frac{0.929\\ \\mathrm{m^3/event}}\n"
"  {\\left(70\\ \\mathrm{m^3/day}\\right)\n"
"   \\left(18\\ \\mathrm{h/event}\\right)\n"
"   \\left(1\\ \\mathrm{day}/24\\ \\mathrm{h}\\right)}\n"
"= 0.0177\n"
"= 1.77\\%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:255
msgid "Equation :eq:`residuals_daily_backwash_volume` then gives the average daily backwash volume:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:257
msgid "\\forall_{b,d}\n"
"= F_b Q_p t_d\n"
"= \\left(0.0177\\right)\n"
"  \\left(70\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{m^3}}{\\mathrm{day}}\\right)\n"
"= 1.24\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{m^3}}{\\mathrm{day}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:266
msgid "Preliminary estimates of backwash-water quality are **10–50 NTU** and **10–50 mg/L TSS**. If the clarifier effluent turbidity is :math:`T_{\\mathrm{clar}}=0.5\\ \\mathrm{NTU}` and the filter effluent turbidity is :math:`T_{\\mathrm{fi}}=0.1\\ \\mathrm{NTU}`, the filter removes a turbidity equivalent of :math:`0.4\\ \\mathrm{NTU}`. Assuming this captured-solids concentration is conserved and released in the backwash fraction, the estimated backwash turbidity is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:268
msgid "T_b\n"
"\\approx \\frac{T_{\\mathrm{clar}}-T_{\\mathrm{fi}}}{F_b}\n"
"= \\frac{0.5\\ \\mathrm{NTU}-0.1\\ \\mathrm{NTU}}{0.0177}\n"
"= 22.6\\ \\mathrm{NTU}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:276
msgid "where :math:`T_b` is the estimated backwash turbidity. This estimate falls within the preliminary range above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:278
msgid "The formulas assume stable plant flow and a representative backwash interval. The actual event discharge hydrograph is needed to size conveyance or equalization facilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:280
msgid "At an assumed backwash concentration :math:`C_b` (kg/m³), the solids discharged per event are"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:282
msgid "M_b = \\forall_b C_b"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:289
msgid ":math:`M_b` is the solids discharged per backwash event, in kg/event;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:290
msgid ":math:`\\forall_b` is the backwash volume per event, in m³/event; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:291
msgid ":math:`C_b` is the flow-weighted backwash solids concentration, in kg/m³."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:293
msgid "The actual solids concentration changes during a backwash, so a flow-weighted composite sample is preferable to a single grab sample."
