msgid "Coagulant-derived elemental-aluminum mass fraction of the dry residual solids as a function of average raw-water turbidity. The curve uses Equation :eq:`residuals_aluminum_mass_fraction` and the preliminary coefficients listed in the solids-production section. This graph is based on the assumed dosing model and preliminary coefficients. Actual aluminum mass fraction may vary significantly with source water characteristics, coagulant product, and operating conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:344
msgid "Other Discharge Characteristics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:346
msgid "**pH:** The pH of both streams is expected to be near raw-water pH, but coagulant chemistry and operating conditions can cause differences. Verify when pH is relevant to disposal approval."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:347
msgid "**Other treatment chemicals:** AguaClara uses an aluminum coagulant (such as polyaluminum chloride or aluminum sulfate); no separate polymer flocculant is normally added. The coagulant contributes aluminum hydroxide solids. Chlorine is generally dosed after filtration and is not normally a major constituent of clarifier purges or filter backwash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:348
msgid "**Hydraulics:** For the PF70 configuration described here, discharge pipe outlets are near the plant floor. Actual outlet elevations, pipe sizes, and discharge connections must be documented for each plant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Residuals/Residuals_Generation_and_Management.rst:349
msgid "**Management options:** Depending on local requirements, residuals may be settled or thickened before further handling, with clarified supernatant managed separately. Reuse, irrigation, wetland treatment, or discharge to a receiving water requires site-specific evaluation and regulatory approval."
msgstr ""
